# L §5.11 (PL-11): "A def keyed by an index of days is read at any computed day of its range (`f[d]`); a day outside
# it is `RUN-KEY`." f is keyed by a day index of January, g by the built-in days of the run (2026). At d0 + 3 =
# 2026-01-13 both give days_between(2026-01-01, 2026-01-13) = 12 (q); at d0 + 30 = 2026-02-09, outside f's index:
# RUN-KEY (q2); at d0 + 400 = 2027-02-14, outside days: RUN-KEY (q3); L §8.4 `<d> is outside the days of <def>`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input d0: date
input n: int
input d1: date
index ds = day 2026-01-01..2026-01-31
def f[d in ds]: int = days_between(d1, d)
def g[d in days]: int = days_between(d1, d)

ask q: f[add_days(d0, n)], g[add_days(d0, n)]
ask q2: f[add_days(d0, n)] with n = 30
ask q3: g[add_days(d0, n)] with n = 400

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d0 = 2026-01-10
  n = 3
  d1 = 2026-01-01
=== expect
q: (12, 12)
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: refused: RUN-KEY 2026-02-09 is outside the days of f
  pinned: n = 30
  cut 2026-12-31
q3: refused: RUN-KEY 2027-02-14 is outside the days of g
  pinned: n = 400
  cut 2026-12-31
